; Allows com.microsoft.windows.systemapp (transplanted from the reference Microsoft
; image, see docs/architecture.md) to register and
; find its custom IWsaSystemApp service via service_manager.
;
; The type and the first three rules are copied verbatim from the reference
; system_ext_sepolicy.cil of image 2407.40000.4.0 (found
; 18.09.2026 while bringing up the network). The last line (membership in the
; service_manager_type attribute) was MISSED in the first transplant and found
; separately: without it system_app cannot find ITS OWN service
; (the broad rule `allow system_app service_manager_type:service_manager
; find` in system/sepolicy/private/system_app.te only applies to members of
; this attribute).
;
; WARNING: like wsa_vendor_compat.cil, this file is not wired into the build
; automatically via SYSTEM_EXT_PRIVATE_SEPOLICY_DIRS (that variable
; accepts only .te files compiled at build time, not raw CIL,
; which secilc processes at device boot) — it is still wired in
; by a manual post-patch of the already built system_ext_sepolicy.cil
; (bin/patch-system-file.sh).
(type wsa_systemapp_service)
(roletype object_r wsa_systemapp_service)
(allow priv_app wsa_systemapp_service (service_manager (find)))
(allow system_app wsa_systemapp_service (service_manager (add)))
(allow system_server wsa_systemapp_service (service_manager (find)))
(typeattributeset service_manager_type (wsa_systemapp_service))
